Expected elements: present

All backbone items are on the page: provenance banner above the identity bar (badge, `aztec` slug, producer prose), slim identity bar with the chain-targeting exit `← aztec`, hash, stepping controls in both directions, scrubber, phase rail and the `NOIR` tag; Code pane positioned at line 32; Call Trace and Event Log as one tabbed region with Call Trace open and eight frames; Values as a separate pane below it; Transaction metadata at right. No spinner, no empty pane, no light chrome, no full-width prose band between the bar and the panes, no page scrollbar.

In layout terms the shell now fits 1080 — the overhang is gone and the vertical spacing reads as one scale (≈7px pane gutters, 16px above the pane row, ≈34px banner padding). Four things still cost rows or break alignment. The banner is 180px (17% of the viewport) for a 590px prose measure — 31% of a full-width band — so ~80px is recoverable by widening the measure and inlining the badge, and that 80px lands directly on the Code and Transaction panes, which are the two cut off at the floor. Those two end on a half-rendered row at the exact viewport edge with no bottom rule and no scrollbar, so the floor reads as a crop; Values ends on a completed row. The Call Trace region is ~48% blank below "By call order." while Values has ~67px slack. Value chips in Code are anchored two ways, and the Transaction pane handles hash overflow three ways.

Fix first: reclaim banner rows; give the pane column a bottom edge.

Rating: 7/10

